#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
workspace-labels — one short label per Hyprland workspace, shown in a popup
under the bar when he switches workspaces (2026-11-02).

Docs: docs/workspace-labels/ (BRIEF.md = his words, SPEC.md = the card spec,
REPORT.md = what works). His core ask: "the whole point of this is to take
screenshots of workspaces which are not visible also, so that even if I never
switch on them, their summary gets created."

STAGE 1  capture: every window of every workspace (hidden ones too) is grabbed
         with `grim -T <stableId>` (ext-image-copy-capture of a foreign
         toplevel; Hyprland's `stableId` in `hyprctl clients -j` IS the
         ext-foreign-toplevel identifier) and composited at its hyprctl
         position into one workspace image. A window that does not answer in
         CAPTURE_TIMEOUT (paused mpv) is drawn as a title card instead.
STAGE 2  detectors: socket2 openwindow/closewindow/movewindow (resize is
         ignored), terminal foreground program (/proc), window class set; an
         activity signal (evdev timestamps only, never which key) per focused
         window; 10-minute refresh of workspaces he is working on.
STAGE 3  labeller: `claude -p --model sonnet` with a plain-English prompt and
         the workspace image, one at a time, never two for the same workspace,
         gated by the shared USD 200/week agent-loop ledger on the desktop.
STAGE 4+ popup (GTK3 layer shell, top centre under the bar, no focus, clicks
         pass through except on the popup itself, dismissed by the first input
         after 400 ms): the plain label, the live agent card (SPEC.md) when
         there is no label yet, and the old label over the running agent on a
         relabel.
         LOCK (his 2026-11-09, rules narrowed 2026-11-10): Super pressed ALONE
         and held LOCK_HOLD_S (a hold in which any other key was pressed, e.g.
         Super+N switching, never locks) or a tap on the popup LOCKS it: it
         takes exclusive keyboard focus (layer-shell), so Esc reaches IT and
         never a work window, and it stays until Esc / a tap /
         `workspace-labels unlock`. The live card does NOT lock: it ignores
         input for CARD_GRACE_S, then the first input hides it like the label.
         AWAITING (his 2026-11-09): a desk whose windows are all idle (terminal
         at its shell, browser with no page) gets the free title label and no
         model call; it is watched every FAST_POLL s and on title events, and
         relabels the moment work starts (a Claude prompt, a page).

Commands:
  workspace-labels capture [WS ...]   capture + composite (all workspaces if none)
  workspace-labels prompt WS          print the English prompt for a workspace
  workspace-labels label WS           run the labeller once (spends from the ledger)
  workspace-labels daemon             the service (systemd user unit)
  workspace-labels show WS            ask the running daemon to show the popup
  workspace-labels lock | unlock      lock the shown popup (Esc/tap/unlock end it) / release it
  workspace-labels status             labels + capture health as text
"""
